   "status_as_recorded": "untestable",
   "finding": "Connector quality Q_p (teammate-initiated on-off PPP gap) was hypothesized to be a stable player-season attribute. Observed result: Pearson r(Q_a,Q_b)=+0.215 p=0.0297; Spearman rho=+0.242. Spearman-Brown Q~0.355, S~0.278. Sign agreement 65.7% (67/102) binomial p=0.000996. ICC(player-season)=0.216 (78.4% within). Split-half r=0.215 / SB 0.355 is too low to treat Q_p as a stable scoutable trait; most variance is within-player half-to-half."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-018",
   "status_as_recorded": "inconclusive",
   "finding": "When a defense drops a play type >=0.25 PPP H1 to H2, playsheet counter ranking predicts which alternative scored better in H2 (BEST > SECOND > AVOID). Spearman rho=-0.0639, p=0.099717, n=665 (no clear full-rank signal). Kruskal-Wallis H=32.9723, p=2.7e-05. Mann-Whitney BEST 1.257 (n=56) vs AVOID 1.092 (n=160), U=5546.0, p=0.004018."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF15",
   "status_as_recorded": "artifact",
   "finding": "Opponent PPP rises on the next 1-3 possessions after a star's 2nd personal foul in Q1/Q2. Including FT: lag-1 ATT=+0.204 CI[+0.163,+0.245] (artifact: FT share 41.8% vs 9.9%). Excluding FT: lag-1 +0.0486 [-0.0060,+0.0991] perm p=0.0655; lag-2 -0.0192; lag-3 -0.0272. No lag clears CI+perm+placebo. Raw lag-1 +0.204 (p=0.0005) was 41.8% FT vs 9.9% control. Apples-to-apples +0.049, not significant."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-068",
   "status_as_recorded": "artifact",
   "finding": "PCI (halfcourt PPP + second-chance - TO - transition leakage) explains Net Rating beyond ORtg, Pace, and FGA/poss. A R2=0.763 OOS 0.761; C R2=0.902 OOS 0.919; dR2=+0.139. Offensive-control components add +0.005 R2 beyond ORtg. Net~ORtg+leakage R2=0.948. corr(leakage, DRtg)=+0.894. PCI univariate r=+0.863 vs ORtg +0.866. Headline PCI gain is leakage tracking DRtg (+0.89); offensive-control dR2=+0.005. Baseline omitted defense by construction (Net=ORtg-DRtg)."
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-085",
   "what_failed": "Assessing connector quality Q_p as a stable player-season attribute using split-half reliability (Pearson r, Spearman-Brown, ICC).",
