   "code": "CONFOUNDING",
   "text": "Many factors other than a stable defensive trait can influence H2-H1 changes, including opponent offensive adjustments, score effects, substitution patterns, and coaching changes. These confounders make it difficult to isolate the defense's specific and stable effect."
  },
  {
   "code": "SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER",
   "text": "If the underlying signal of a 'reliable team trait' is weak and noisy, 120 team-seasons may be insufficient to achieve adequate statistical power to establish reliability, especially given the expected low measurement reliability."
  },
  {
   "code": "OUTCOME_DERIVED_LABEL",
   "text": "The 'H2-H1 change' is a derived label from game outcomes, which can be influenced by many factors. Ensuring this measure truly reflects a stable defensive 'effect' is challenging."
  },
  {
   "code": "DRIFT_NONSTATIONARITY",
   "text": "Team strategies, player rosters, and league-wide trends can change over the four seasons of data, potentially affecting the consistency and reliability of any observed 'trait' over time (FAM:SF-APPS-018)."
  }
 ],
 "predicted_outcome": {
  "supported": 0.05,
  "rejected": 0.1,
  "untestable": 0.7,
  "artifact": 0.1,
  "uncertain": 0.05
 },
 "decision": "do_not_proceed",
