  "estimand": "The Intraclass Correlation Coefficient (ICC) of a defense's effect on opponents' H2-H1 change in points per possession (PPP) across multiple games within the same team-season, and across different team-seasons for the same team.",
  "unit": "Team-season for assessing across-season reliability; Game for assessing within-season reliability. The base unit for 'H2-H1 change' will be a single game's H2 PPP minus H1 PPP for the opponent.",
  "sample": "All 120 available team-seasons (NBA 2022-23 to 2025-26). For each team-season, include all regular season and playoff games. Exclude games with significant garbage time in either half (e.g., score differential > 20 points in the last 5 minutes of a half).",
  "power": "Not estimable with confidence due to predicted low reliability. A minimum of 0.8 power for detecting an ICC of 0.5 would likely require a significantly larger sample of team-seasons or games per team-season than available.",
  "controls": "To isolate 'defense's effect' on H2-H1 change, a robust counterfactual model would be needed. This would involve controlling for: opponent offensive strength (e.g., H1 ORtg, season average ORtg), game state (e.g., score differential at halftime, pace), player availability (injuries, foul trouble), substitution patterns, and coaching changes. A simpler approach would be to measure raw H2-H1 opponent PPP change and calculate its reliability, acknowledging it conflates defensive and offensive factors.",
  "falsification": "A null hypothesis of ICC <= 0.2 (based on FAM:SF-APPS-085) for the H2-H1 change measure, suggesting the trait is not reliable. If the calculated ICC is significantly greater than 0.2 with sufficient power, the trait might be considered reliable.",
  "multiplicity": "Not applicable if focusing solely on the reliability of one specific metric.",
  "decision_rule": "The research question would be deemed 'supported' if the ICC for the defense's effect on opponents' H2-H1 change is statistically significantly (p < 0.05) above a predefined threshold for 'reliable' (e.g., ICC > 0.5), with sufficient power. Otherwise, it would be 'rejected' (if adequately powered) or 'untestable' (if reliability is too low, as anticipated).",
  "data_version": "NBA 2022-23 to 2025-26 regular season and playoffs, as of 2026-10-06."
 }
}

